{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Release critique lens B (operator surface and failure messaging) for the pending 8.9.5 patch","packet_sha256":"0ea96d3103bf2304fa335063cfa0bab2d3bc61ccd1c01612f7834e1d771e350a","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"294d9fb8d4ed1d5c262526b0fcf87ac48445f5b4ec54c87f4237f741e3e2abd7","verdict":"block","target_observations":[{"target":"task-run-persist-scope","verdict":"pass","summary":"Candidate persistence is restricted to scope-admitted paths and fails closed when residue prevents a complete carrier.","evidence":["scripts/task_run/task_run_completion.py passes `_in_scope_candidate_paths(candidate)` to `persist_incomplete_candidate`.","scripts/task_run/task_run_lane_runner.py excludes `disallowed_paths`, skips an empty admitted set, and documents that out-of-scope residue must not enter the commit.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_completion.py verifies allowed-only commits, all-disallowed skips, and retained dirty residue."]},{"target":"release-resume-notes-placeholder","verdict":"pass","summary":"Ambiguous drafted notes are represented as an explicit operator placeholder, while a unique candidate is inserted verbatim and absence emits no notes flag.","evidence":["skills/public/release/scripts/plan_release_run_packets.py emits `--notes-file <notes-file>` when multiple drafted-note candidates exist and records `<notes-file>` in `placeholders`.","tests/quality_gates/test_release_run_planner_prepared_stop.py covers the multiple, single, and zero-candidate cases."]},{"target":"staged-eviction-owner","verdict":"pass","summary":"The staged owner selects eligible test files and its refusal names both the unsafe operation and the safe replacement.","evidence":["scripts/hooks/check_staged_cheap_owners.py dispatches `check-module-eviction-form (staged)` from the full staged Python set after the eviction owner's own target selection.","scripts/gates/check_module_eviction_form.py reports the file, count, line/form sites, and directs the operator to `tests/module_eviction.py` using `evict_module` or `evict_new_modules` so parent-package attributes are not stranded.","tests/quality_gates/test_module_eviction_form_gate.py and tests/quality_gates/test_staged_cheap_owners.py cover staged selection, refusal text, exclusions, and hook dispatch."]},{"target":"worker-expected-targets","verdict":"block","summary":"Expected targets reach finalization, but the bound input does not establish that the resulting coverage refusal identifies the precise coverage mistake and gives an actionable remedy.","evidence":["skills/shared/scripts/run_reviewer_worker.py forwards `args.expected_target` to `finalize_attempt(... expected_targets=...)`.","The implementation of imported `reviewer_runner_support.finalize_attempt` is not included in the semantic input, so the actual coverage-error construction and operator message cannot be reviewed.","tests/quality_gates/test_reviewer_runner.py asserts only that the reason contains `expected targets`; it does not require missing, duplicate, extra, empty-summary, or empty-evidence details, nor instructions to emit exactly one substantive observation per declared target."]},{"target":"prepared-target-worker-wiring","verdict":"pass","summary":"The live semantic-review path validates the packet declaration and translates every prepared target into a worker `--expected-target` argument.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_execution.py validates that `prepared_targets` is a list of nonblank strings before constructing the live worker command.","skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_invocation.py appends one `--expected-target` argument for every prepared target.","tests/quality_gates/test_review_target_coverage_floor.py exercises the live wrapper and demonstrates refusal when a declared target is omitted and eligibility when it is observed."]},{"target":"lane-target-declaration","verdict":"pass","summary":"The generated reviewer prompt declares the target set and requires one substantive observation per target without claiming that labels expand reviewed scope.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_packet.py renders the prepared-target list and requires exactly one observation with a nonempty summary and evidence array for each target.","skills/public/critique/references/prepare-packet.md states that labels do not expand reviewed content and distinguishes automatic wrapper behavior from the low-level worker interface.","tests/quality_gates/test_review_target_coverage_floor.py verifies that the dry-run prompt names the target and the exactly-one requirement."]}],"findings":[{"id":"RC-B-001","severity":"high","summary":"The coverage-refusal operator contract is not reviewable or strongly tested in this packet, so the release cannot establish that coverage failures name the mistake and remedy.","evidence":["The only reviewed worker call site delegates coverage judgment and messaging to `reviewer_runner_support.finalize_attempt`, whose implementation is absent from the reviewed paths.","The end-to-end assertions require only `coverage_ok is False`, the expected-target list, and the substring `expected targets`.","Those assertions permit a vague refusal that does not identify which targets are missing or malformed and does not tell the operator to emit exactly one nonempty observation for each declared target."],"action":"Bind the coverage/finalization implementation into the review and add assertions that each refusal identifies the offending target condition and tells the operator how to repair it; then rerun this release critique."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The preparation reference tells low-level users to repeat `--expected-target`, while the normal `run_review.py` wrapper wires targets automatically.","bin":"non-blocking wording risk","disposition":"The surrounding prose identifies `run_review.py` as the normal path and the low-level worker as a compatibility interface; the actual automatic wiring matches the live wrapper behavior."},{"concern":"Path-scoped eviction checks return success when none of the explicit paths belongs to the eviction universe.","bin":"intentional behavior","disposition":"This is a precise staged selection, not a broad-scan coverage claim; tests explicitly distinguish it from the whole-universe empty refusal."},{"concern":"Ambiguous notes placeholders make emitted commands non-runnable until edited.","bin":"required operator stop","disposition":"The placeholder and `placeholders` metadata truthfully expose an unresolved choice instead of emitting a runnable-looking command that the notes preflight will refuse."}],"next_move":"Add the coverage-finalization owner to the bound semantic input, strengthen its refusal contract tests to require the specific mistake and remedy, and rerun the bounded release critique before shipping 8.9.5.","non_claims":["No workspace files were read or modified; the judgment uses only the identity-bound inline payload.","No test suite or release command was executed.","This review does not claim the omitted coverage-finalization implementation is defective; it finds the required operator-facing behavior unestablished by the reviewed release input.","Goal evidence lineage is not goal-bound."]}
